                            1
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَنَاهُ</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>He tried him; proved him.</i> (S, K.)
You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَنَاهُ اللّٰهُ بِحُبِّهَا</span>
                        <i>God tried him by love
of her.</i> (T.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُنِىَ بِكَذَا</span>
                        <i>He was tried by
such a thing.</i> (T.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَنَى</span>
                        <i>He meditated</i> [a
thing in his mind]; syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَدَّرَ</span>. (Bd, ii. 73.) See
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَمِنْيَّةٌ</span>.

